{
 "id": "echo-names",
 "version": "0.1",
 "title": "Echo page: the tape echo on one page (TE01)",
 "category": "Examples",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "author": "naturarum",
 "description": "EXPERIMENT. fx-echo 0.2 (dn2-cfw SC01, on a unit) without its flanger sites, so it links with flanger-names: for dn2-cfw's TE01 and later builds, whose DSP runs the tape echo in the delay slot. The delay page and its sends are named Echo/ECHO (the page box says ECH); the page becomes TIME MODE WID FDBK CNTR BW AGE REV: X (Pingpong) widened to MODE 0..6 (heads 1, 2, 3, 12, 23, 13, 123), HPF/LPF named CNTR/BW with the filter picture drawing the echo's band, and the hidden Delay FX Routing row made AGE (0..127, its value shown while it turns) and placed on the empty knob G. Every knob keeps its MIDI CC, storage and DSP frame word; MODE and AGE are never p-lockable; AGE has no CC. On a stock DSP the names would be wrong.",
 "device": "digitone-mk2",
 "os": "1.12",
 "sources": [
  "echo_names.c",
  "graph.s"
 ],
